    <!--
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        THEME: Neon Cyber LED — dark, LED-strip borders, cyan/magenta glow, scanline/grid accents.
        Owner-approved design: E:\cluadex-bld\research\themes\NeonMain.dc.html
        (picker preview: ThemePicker.dc.html — #070812 grid, #00E5FF strips, #FF2BD6 / #A6FF00 glow).

        STARTS AS A COPY OF Midnight.xaml (theme foundation) — the Neon Cyber theme team replaces the values.
        Rules (tests/themetest enforces the first two):
          • Keep EXACTLY the keys Midnight.xaml has — no key only one theme defines, same kind of value.
          • Theme.Id stays "NeonCyber".
          • Fill the SEMANTIC TOKENS first (they drive Theme.xaml's controls and every converted view);
            the LEGACY PALETTE only matters for views not converted yet.
          • Glows are this theme's identity — keep them as DropShadowEffect tokens, never inline.
        ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    -->

    <sys:String x:Key="Theme.Id">NeonCyber</sys:String>

